<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Hashing hides the codes, but doesn&rsquo;t make them secret.</strong> A six-digit code has a million possibilities, and anyone holding the document can hash all of them in seconds and find the match. Keep the document&rsquo;s URL private, and use longer codes where it matters.</li>
		<li><strong>No lockout.</strong> Each wrong guess ends the call, but nothing stops someone from calling again. Watch your call logs for repeated failures.</li>
		<li><strong>The caller&rsquo;s number isn&rsquo;t checked.</strong> To require both a code and a known number, add the number lists from the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-call-screening-with-voiceml/">call screening example</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>Changing a code means publishing again.</strong> Published documents can&rsquo;t be edited, so a new code is a new document and a new URL for the number.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

